1
00:03:36,428 --> 00:03:42,428
Everybody has a soul. Joe Gardner is about to find his.

2
00:07:12,857 --> 00:07:18,857
Soul is a animation, family, comedy film directed by Pete Docter.

3
00:10:49,285 --> 00:10:55,285
Joe Gardner is a middle school teacher with a love for jazz music.

4
00:14:25,714 --> 00:14:31,714
After a successful audition at the Half Note Club, he suddenly gets into an accident that separates his soul from his body and is
transported to the You Seminar, a center in which souls develop and gain passions before being transported to a newborn child.

5
00:18:02,142 --> 00:18:08,142
Joe must enlist help from the other souls-in-training, like 22, a soul who has
spent eons in the You Seminar, in order to get back to Earth.

6
00:21:38,571 --> 00:21:44,571
Joe Gardner (voice), played by Jamie Foxx.

7
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:21,000
22 (voice), played by Tina Fey.

8
00:28:51,428 --> 00:28:57,428
Moonwind (voice), played by Graham Norton.

9
00:32:27,857 --> 00:32:33,857
Terry (voice), played by Rachel House.

10
00:36:04,285 --> 00:36:10,285
Counselor Jerry (voice), played by Alice Braga.

11
00:39:40,714 --> 00:39:46,714
Counselor Jerry (voice), played by Richard Ayoade.

12
00:43:17,142 --> 00:43:23,142
Soul is a 2020 American animated fantasy comedy-drama film produced
by Pixar Animation Studios for Walt Disney Pictures.

13
00:46:53,571 --> 00:46:59,571
Directed by Pete Docter, who co-wrote it with Mike Jones and Kemp Powers, the film stars the voices of Jamie Foxx, Tina Fey, Graham
Norton, Rachel House, Alice Braga, Richard Ayoade, Phylicia Rashad, Donnell Rawlings, Questlove, and Angela Bassett.

14
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:36,000
It follows Joe Gardner (Foxx), a middle school teacher and aspiring pianist who falls into a coma following an
accident and seeks to reunite his separated soul and body in time for his big break as a jazz musician.

15
00:54:06,428 --> 00:54:12,428
Docter conceived Soul in January 2016, examining the origins of
human personalities and the concept of determinism.

16
00:57:42,857 --> 00:57:48,857
During his first meeting with Jones, he pitched the idea about
spacetime involving souls with personalities.

17
01:01:19,285 --> 01:01:25,285
The film's producers consulted various jazz musicians, including Herbie Hancock and Terri Lyne Carrington,
and animated its musical sequences using the sessions of musician Jon Batiste as a reference.

18
01:04:55,714 --> 01:05:01,714
Apart from Batiste's original jazz compositions, musicians Trent
Reznor and Atticus Ross composed the film's score.

19
01:08:32,142 --> 01:08:38,142
Production on Soul lasted for four years on an approximate $150 million budget.

20
01:12:08,571 --> 01:12:14,571
It was the first Pixar film to feature a black lead.

21
01:15:45,000 --> 01:15:51,000
Soul premiered at the BFI London Film Festival on October 11, 2020, and was scheduled for theatrical
release on June 19 and November 20; however, it was postponed due to the COVID-19 pandemic.

22
01:19:21,428 --> 01:19:27,428
It was released direct-to-streaming on Disney+ on December 25, 2020, accompanied by the
short film Burrow, and in theaters in countries without the streaming service.

23
01:22:57,857 --> 01:23:03,857
It was theatrically released in the United States on January 12, 2024,
and grossed over $122 million at the worldwide box office.

24
01:26:34,285 --> 01:26:40,285
The National Board of Review and the American Film Institute
named Soul one of the top ten films of 2020.

25
01:30:10,714 --> 01:30:16,714
It was nominated for three Academy Awards at the 93rd Academy Awards,
winning two, and received numerous other accolades.

26
01:33:47,142 --> 01:33:53,142
The film explores themes of new york city, jazz, musician, cat, self-discovery.

27
01:37:23,571 --> 01:37:29,571
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
